hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"279","Na Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al Makhzoumi, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al Qasim bin Muhammad, he said: I asked Aisha about A man comes to his family, wears a garment, and sweats impurity from it. Is that? She said: “The woman was preparing a rag or rags, and if that was the case, the man would wipe away the dirt on him with it, and he did not see that that would defile him.”"
"280","Muhammad bin Maymun Al-Makki narrated to me, Al-Walid, meaning the son of Muslim, narrated to me. Al-Awza’i narrated to me, Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Qasim narrated to me, on the authority of his father Al-Qasim. Ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “A woman takes a rag, and when her husband is finished, she hands it to him.” So he wiped off the dirt from him, and she wiped off it, then they prayed in their clothes.”"
